{"type": "thinking", "text": "Unfavoriting removed it and empty state shows. Reversal works.\n\nNow, the bottom nav label \"Videos\" while on Favorites is suspicious. Let me check whether this happens across app restart or is just per-session remember. Also, if the Media tab label becomes \"Videos\", that's likely a genuine visual bug to report. But I should verify it's reproducible: with Photos chip, label \"Photos\"; Videos chip, \"Videos\". Let me test again after switching chip to Photos and nav to Favorites.\n\nActually, from the earlier screenshot of Albums (when Media chip selected), bottom let nav label was \"Photos\" (element [11] \"Photos\" @(127,2169)). Wait — in the Albums screen observation right after opening Albums from Media with Photos chip selected, element [11] was \"View contains 'Photos' [clickable] @(127,2169)\". So yes the first nav tab said \"Photos\" while the Albums tab was active. So the first tab label tracks the Media chip. Is that a bug? Hmm. This might be intended behavior in this app's design? Some apps (e.g., Google Photos) don't do that. But this app's nav label reflecting active content-type filter is weird.\n\nWait... maybe it's not the nav label; maybe the bottom nav has a dynamically labeled \"Media/Photos/Videos\" tab by design, where selecting chip changes the section name. Hmm, that's plausible: the \"Media\" tab hosts Media, Photos, Videos views. The chip changes what's shown and the tab is renamed accordingly. But then Favorites tab showing \"Videos\" is consistent with the chosen Media content type — still weird UX but maybe by design.\n\nAlternatively, this is exactly the injected regression: moving chip state from settings to screen-level caused the nav label to be replaced. Hmm.\n\nLet me look for more obvious bugs. Let's test favorites query \"same data source as Media tab\". In Media with Videos chip, Favorites still showed photo. But what if we favorite a photo while Media chip is Photos then switch to Videos and check Favorites? Already fine.\n\nPotential bug: the Favorites grid should show only favorited items but might show items from all albums incorrectly? We saw 1 of 1 correct.\n\nMaybe favorites doesn't update when toggling from Favorites viewer? We tested: empty after unfavorite. Good.\n\nLet's test favoriting second item (hughugeQ.jpg) and count. Also check duplicate names: two big.jpg (Beta and apple). If we favorite apple/big.jpg, Favorites would show two big.jpg. That's expected since they're distinct files. To identify, maybe viewer header shows path. Not a bug.\n\nImportant: The Media tab may not be sorted correctly; but not in scope.\n\nNow the album count feature. Let me test adding a favorite doesn't change counts. No.\n\nCould test deleting a photo from album to see if album grid count updates. The changed code \"computed once when the album finishes loading\" means if you delete a photo inside the album, the album card count should update upon returning; maybe stale. We'd need to delete a photo (Beta has 2 photos). Deleting is a data change but testing requires it; the task says don't change data outside what testing requires. Deleting then restoring (from trash) is acceptable if reversal tested. The app has trash. Could delete, check count, then restore.\n\nAlternatively use \"Move\" or album creation. Let me check album \"More options\" menu for Beta. Might include \"Set as cover\", \"Rename\", \"Delete\". Hmm.\n\nActually, a simpler test of the count: Go to Albums and toggle the \"Videos\" filter chip. All albums show counts of all items? The count should presumably not change. Or the \"Apps\"/\"Camera & System\" filters may hide albums but counts same.\n\nHmm, wait. Maybe the album item count bug is visible now: the album grid header should show the count of the album's items, but the count appears under album names, and the plugin says \"computed once when the album finishes loading\". Let me check whether the counts are correct: Beta 2 (has big.jpg, hughugeQ.jpg) yes; Zulu 1 (hughugeQ.jpg) yes; apple 1 (big.jpg) yes. Total 4 = media count. So correct.\n\nMaybe the count includes hidden/locked items? no.\n\nWhat about the album grid header showing zero for apple? no.\n\nMaybe there are more photos in an album that aren't displayed due to a limit? Beta shows 2 items and 2 photos. fine.\n\nHmm. Maybe the bug is the *label text* \"1 items\" instead of \"1 item\". The setting says \"Display item numbers under album names\" — grammar with pluralization. It could be a minor bug but is it the injected one? Possibly not.\n\nLet me test more thoroughly the album detail header. The change \"Album grid header: the item count is now computed once when the album finishes loading.\" Perhaps in album detail there should be a header showing \"2 items\", but it doesn't. Hmm, but the setting calls it \"item numbers under album names\", which is the album grid card.\n\nWait, the phrase \"Album grid header\" might mean the header of the album grid screen = the album detail header. In the album detail screen, title \"Beta\" only. In other gallery apps the header shows \"Beta\" and \"2 items\" or date range. The changed behavior \"the item count is now computed once when the album finishes loading\" implies there's a visible item count somewhere on load. The only visible counts are under album names. I'll treat those.\n\nNow let's test deleting an item to see if the count updates. But wait — maybe the bug is simpler: after adding a favorite or something the count changes? No.\n\nMaybe the count includes the album's cover image twice? Beta cover big.jpg, items 2, correct.\n\nLet me test the albums tab filters: \"Camera & System\", \"Apps\", \"Videos\". These might filter albums and maybe the counts should still be per album. Tap Videos filter → no albums (no videos). Tap Camera & System → maybe shows albums in camera folders? Let's see."}
