{"type": "thinking", "text": "\"huge\" search returns 2 \"hughugeQ.jpg\" items. The name seems to literally contain \"huge\". Hmm, \"hughugeQ.jpg\" contains \"huge\" starting at index 3: h u g h u g e Q — \"huge\" at index 3. So search matches substring. Fine. The weird name may be intentional fixture.\n\nNote: the search is on Photos chip; returns 2 for \"big\" (photos), fine.\n\nLet me test empty search (clear) → back to all 4. Then press back. Search is fine.\n\nNow, focus on finding defects. Let's consider the app might have seeded bugs around these changed areas. Let me re-read the changes:\n\n1. \"Album grid header: the item count is now computed once when the album finishes loading.\" This phrasing suggests previously the count was computed reactively/per item, now once at load. A typical bug: after deleting a photo from an album, the album grid count still shows the old number until app restart. To test, we need to delete a photo and go back to the album grid.\n\n2. \"Favorites grid: favorites are now queried through the same data source as the Media tab.\" Typical bug: favorites might now include items that aren't favorites (e.g., all photos) or exclude some (e.g., filtered by content type). We saw correct. But maybe after favoriting an item from a different album, the favorites grid shows it; yes.\n\nCould be favorites grid doesn't respect the \"Media\" data source being filtered to Videos: if the user selects Videos chip in Media, then Favorites tab might show videos only (or nothing). We tested: Favorites showed the favorited photos while Videos chip was selected. So no.\n\nCould be favorites grid duplicates items due to join query across sources. We have 2 favorites; no duplicates. Add a third/fourth favorite and check no dupes. We'll add apple/big.jpg and Zulu/hughugeQ.jpg as favorites, then Favorites should show 4 items. Let's see if duplicates appear (maybe each media source row duplicated by join). This is worth testing.\n\n3. \"Media tab content-type chips: the chosen chip is now tracked by the screen rather than in the app's settings.\" Typical bug: chip selection resets when switching tabs or rotation or process death. We saw it persists across tabs and rotation. Hmm. But maybe it resets after app is backgrounded/killed? \"tracked by the screen\" with `remember` would survive recomposition but not process death. Hard to test process death. We could use app switch and return? That doesn't kill.\n\nWait — maybe the bug is that chips are tracked at app-level screen state shared with the Settings \"Default Startup Tab\"? Or the chip selection changes the bottom nav label (found). This seems the visible defect.\n\nActually, maybe the bug is that the selected chip persists to the album screen's chip row? No.\n\nHmm, let me consider that the bottom nav label changing may be intended \"the chosen chip is now tracked by the screen\" → the bottom tab becomes the content type, i.e., they intentionally reflect the chip in the nav bar. But then the nav bar label changes only on the Media screen (top). Seeing \"Videos\" on Favorites is because the nav is global. Would a dev design that? Unlikely.\n\nLet me look at the Library tab maybe has \"Media\" label? The Settings lists tabs Media/Albums/Favorites/Library. The bottom first tab is clearly \"Media\". Changing to \"Photos\" is a bug: the Media tab label should remain Media. But is it possible the app intentionally renames the tab to the filter because Media/Photos/Videos are \"content types\" and the tab is actually showing the selected type? I'm leaning it's a bug.\n\nLet me test another angle: Default startup tab setting. Settings says Default Startup Tab = Media. If I choose \"Favorites\" and relaunch, the app should start on Favorites. Not in scope though.\n\nLet me now test the album count through deletion. Plan:\n- Go to Albums root (Beta etc.).\n- Open Beta album, select big.jpg, delete it (default action Trash, confirm before deleting is OFF, use system trash OFF → private in-app trash).\n- Return to album grid: Beta count should become \"1 items\". Since count computed once when album finishes loading, maybe the album card still shows 2 items (stale) — that's the bug.\n- Then restore from trash if possible (Library > Trash). If not restorable, we changed data. Hmm. \"Do not change data outside what testing requires.\" Deleting for a test is arguably required. But maybe I can instead add a new photo to an album? Hard without file system access.\n\nAlternative: favorite status changes shouldn't affect count. Could use \"Move to album\" if available? In viewer More selection actions maybe \"Move\". Moving a photo from Beta to Zulu would change both counts. Reversible by moving back. But still need to see if counts update.\n\nActually, deleting seems the direct way. But restoring may be possible via Library > Trash → Restore. Let's check Library tab first non-destructively to see trash exists. Let me cancel search first."}
