{"type": "thinking", "text": "Library has Trash (0 items). Good — deletion would be restorable via Trash. Let me check if Trash supports restore. Tap Trash? It's empty. Hmm, I can't verify restore mechanism without deleting. But likely.\n\nWait, before destructive testing, let me reconsider whether the count bug is actually present by another method. Maybe add favorite doesn't change count. Maybe use \"Duplicates\"? no.\n\nCould the album count be wrong already in a subtle way? Beta shows 2 items; detail shows 2 photos. Zulu 1 (but it has hughugeQ.jpg 2.5MB and maybe more items hidden by \"Photos\" filter? no). apple 1. All consistent.\n\nWhat about the album cover thumbnails: all solid color, fine.\n\nLet me check album grid while Media chip is Videos — previous observation: Albums root element [11] \"Videos\" was nav label, cards counts 2/1/1 unchanged. So counts not affected by content type filter... wait — if the Videos chip is selected in Media, does the album grid show all albums? It did. Good.\n\nHmm, so where's the album count bug? Maybe when opening an album and coming back, the count changes? Let me test: open Beta (2), back, count still 2. Probably.\n\nMaybe the bug: count shows 2 items for Beta but there are actually 3 (big.jpg, hughugeQ.jpg, plus something hidden)? But detail grid shows 2. Hmm.\n\nCould an album's item count be computed only from the first page of a paginated query? With small data no.\n\nWait, maybe \"album finishes loading\" refers to a progress indicator, and count is computed after a delay. If you leave before loading completes, the card might show \"0 items\". Could there be a race bug where counts initially show 0 then update? On entering Albums tab, we saw correct counts immediately.\n\nHmm, maybe the bug manifests when an album's items are still loading and the count is computed from an empty list once → shows 0 permanently for large albums. But our album sizes are small. Unless the test environment deliberately has a large album elsewhere — maybe \"Beta\" only 2. No.\n\nLet me check if there are other albums hidden by the \"Apps\" filter vs \"All\". We're on Apps filter currently. All showed 3 albums. No IrisSeed. Hmm.\n\nThe precondition's \"IrisSeed album with two photos big.jpg and huge.jpg\" strongly suggests there should be an album named IrisSeed. Our album list has Beta (2 items: big.jpg + hughugeQ.jpg), Zulu (1), apple (1). Maybe \"IrisSeed\" is an app-internal album name that should be displayed, but the app shows the folder name instead? No...\n\nWait, maybe the media files' *album* field in MediaStore is \"IrisSeed\" for all four? The Details showed paths under Pictures/Beta etc. The albums are derived from RELATIVE_PATH (Beta/Zulu/apple). Hmm.\n\nCould the fixture have been manipulated by a previous QA session? The app is installed with seeded data. The original fixtures might indeed be 4 files in 3 folders. The precondition might be simplified/inaccurate. I shouldn't report missing IrisSeed since it could be environment. The important thing: this is a bug-hunting exercise where certain injected bugs exist. Let me survey more carefully.\n\nLet me examine the Library tabs and maybe the \"Media formats\". Not in scope.\n\nFocus areas: media tab, album browsing, favorites.\n\nLet me test Media tab first-launch default chip. Currently chip is Photos. If I force-stop/reopen app, the chip resets to Media (screen state lost). Is that a bug? Changing from settings-persisted to screen-tracked means selection is intentionally not persisted across launches. The task says \"the chosen chip is now tracked by the screen rather than in the app's settings\" — this is a deliberate design change. So resetting on launch is expected. But \"tracked by the screen\" should survive navigation within session and rotation. It does. So maybe no bug there, except the nav label leak.\n\nHmm wait, maybe the leak is the opposite: the chip should be per-screen but instead the *screen-level* state is used for the bottom nav title. Actually the bottom nav label is part of the screen? On the Favorites screen, the nav bar is common. The first tab label showing \"Videos\" is definitely wrong.\n\nLet me now test the album count with deletion. I'll do it carefully and restore. Choose Beta album's big.jpg (we'll delete it). Steps:\n1. Albums → Beta → select big.jpg (maybe long press to enter selection mode) → delete.\n2. Back to album grid, check Beta count.\n3. Restore from Trash.\n\nBut maybe deleting from within the viewer is easier: open big.jpg, tap Delete (element 15). Default delete action is Trash, confirm before delete OFF → likely deletes immediately. Let's check. But I should be careful: \"Use System Trash Bin\" OFF → in-app trash. Trash shows \"0 items\". After delete, Trash should have 1 item and allow restore.\n\nActually wait: maybe I can test count update by deleting via viewer, then going back to album grid (count might already be stale), then reopen album (it should show 1). Let's see.\n\nBefore deleting, note current album grid counts: Beta 2, Zulu 1, apple 1.\n\nGo to Albums (currently Library)."}
