{"type": "thinking", "text": "Uh oh! After restoring huge.jpg, the IrisSeed album is now split into TWO album cards: \"huge.jpg | IrisSeed | 1 items\" and \"big.jpg | IrisSeed | 1 items\"! Before deleting, IrisSeed was one album with 2 items. After delete+restore, the restored file created a second IrisSeed album card. So the restore operation splits the album. This is the same class of bug as move: moving/restoring a file into an existing folder creates a duplicate album entry with the same name.\n\nWait, actually maybe this happened because the trash restore reinserted the file with a new bucket ID, splitting the album. So the album list now has 7 cards? Let's count: IrisSeed(huge) 1, IrisSeed(big) 1, Beta(big (1)) 1, Zulu 1, apple 1, Beta(hughugeQ) 1 = 6 cards, 6 items. So now every \"2 items\" album got split! Beta split earlier due to move, IrisSeed split due to restore. So the album grouping bug is triggered by re-inserting files (move or restore) — the app fails to merge into existing album.\n\nHmm, that's a real bug but not necessarily the seeded one. But it's reproducible: delete+restore causes album split. However, it's about the delete/restore feature, not the sweep areas. Yet the visible symptom is duplicate album cards in album browsing. Hmm.\n\nWait, maybe this is *because* \"Album grid header: the item count is now computed once when the album finishes loading\"? No.\n\nHmm, hold on. Maybe the app defines an album as a *folder path*, and the restored file went to a different folder? Let's check the restored path. The details before delete: /storage/emulated/0/Pictures/IrisSeed/huge.jpg. After restore, maybe it went to /storage/emulated/0/Pictures/IrisSeed/ with a new bucket ID due to how the app re-inserts. The album card shows \"huge.jpg | IrisSeed\". So display name same.\n\nI think this app has a genuine \"album identity\" bug: album IDs are derived from something unstable (e.g., the bucket ID assigned at scan). Re-inserted files get a new bucket ID, so the album splits. But the app's album *display name* is computed from the latest file's bucket display name. So duplicate cards.\n\nWait, actually maybe the *MediaStore bucket id* differs for the re-inserted file because the app's trash/restore writes it to a different folder then moves? No, path should be IrisSeed.\n\nI need to be careful: Could the restored huge.jpg be in *private app storage* (vault/trash) instead of Pictures/IrisSeed, yet the album card still says IrisSeed? The restore said \"Item restored to gallery\". Let me check its details path. Also check media tab count.\n\nThis duplicate-album behavior is definitely a bug visible in album browsing. But is it caused by the \"Album grid header item count computed once\" change? Possibly: if album entries are cached and counts computed at load, the new album record... no.\n\nLet me check whether the duplicate cards merge if I rescan (Settings → Rescan media library). That might rebuild albums from MediaStore correctly. If rescan merges them, it's just the app's incremental update bug. Let me try the rescan to restore the data (merge duplicates) — useful. But it's a lot of scrolling. Maybe I can use Settings from the Albums screen icon (element 9) and scroll to bottom quickly with multiple large swipes, but the tool warns about repeated identical swipes. I can vary distances.\n\nAlternatively, use the \"More options\" in Albums (element 9 in the album card? no, [9] is Settings). Let me first check Media tab count: should be 6. Tap Photos nav (element 10)."}
