{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed: bottom nav first tab is labeled \"Videos\" with a play icon. The tab should be \"Media\". This is visible in the Media screen too. Report it.\n\nBut is it possible this is intended? Let me check the Settings \"Navigation tabs\" list: it says \"Media\" checked. And Default Startup Tab says \"Media\". So the nav item is named Media elsewhere. The nav item changes label dynamically. I'd call it a bug: \"tab label changes with content filter, inconsistent with Settings and unclear navigation.\" symptom_type: wrong_value (shown text). Element_ref: 5.\n\nLet me file this report now.\n\nReport fields:\n- screen: \"Media tab (bottom navigation bar)\"\n- element: \"Bottom navigation 'Media' tab label\"\n- field: \"Tab label\"\n- symptom_type: \"wrong_value\"\n- expected: \"The first bottom navigation tab stays labelled 'Media' regardless of the selected content-type chip; chip selection should only affect the Media screen content/title.\"\n- observed: \"With the Videos chip selected, the first bottom navigation tab is labelled 'Videos' (play icon) instead of 'Media'; with Photos selected it shows 'Photos'. The label also stays 'Videos'/'Photos' while on other tabs such as Favorites.\"\n- steps: [...]\n- element_ref: 5\n- observed_quote: \"Videos\"\n\nCareful: observed_quote must be exact text on screen: \"Videos\". That's valid as the nav label. But the quote \"Videos\" also appears as the title. Still, element_ref 5 points at the nav label. Good.\n\nShould I also mention the state carried to other tabs? The report can mention Favorites screen shows \"Videos\". Steps include selecting Videos then Favorites.\n\nLet me file."}
