{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now, before rescanning, this is a good place to file the \"1 items\" bug. The screen shows multiple \"1 items\" cards: IrisSeed (1 items) x2, Zulu (1 items), apple (1 items). Element_ref 7 (Zulu, \"hughugeQ.jpg | Zulu | 1 items\") or 4. The expected is \"1 item\". Let me decide whether to file.\n\nHmm, \"1 items\" is a minor cosmetic bug. The developer's earlier confirm was for a functional nav bug. Would they confirm \"1 items\"? Probably yes. But is it worth risking? The instructions: \"When you find a bug, file a report.\" I'll file it. It's clearly wrong text and in the album grid header (the changed area mentions album header item count). Actually, this could be exactly the intended album-header bug: the count string is \"1 items\" instead of \"1 item\". The changed build recomputes the count; maybe the pluralization regressed. Let's file.\n\nReport:\n- screen: Albums tab / album grid\n- element: Item-count label under album name (e.g., Zulu card)\n- field: Item count text\n- symptom_type: wrong_value\n- expected: \"1 item\" for a single-item album\n- observed: \"1 items\" is shown under every single-item album (Zulu, apple) as well as in the Move to Album sheet.\n- steps: open Albums; single-item albums show \"1 items\"; open a 2-item album shows \"2 items\"; Move to Album sheet shows \"1 items\" when 1 selected.\n- element_ref: 7\n- observed_quote: \"1 items\"\n\nLet me file."}
