{"type": "thinking", "text": "Confirmed: the restored photo's button says \"Favorite\" (not \"Favorited\"), i.e., the favorite state was lost after trash+restore. This is a real favorites-related bug: restoring a deleted favorite does not restore its favorite status, so it disappears from Favorites. Is it the seeded bug? Possibly. The instructions say favorites are in scope; this is a state/reversal issue. Let me think about expected behavior: \"Reversal: undo, cancel or reverse a change, and check the app returns to the right state.\" Deleting (to trash) and restoring is a reversal. The favorite state should return. It doesn't. This fits the QA guidance well.\n\nBut careful: Is the favorite loss *because* of the \"favorites queried through the same data source as Media tab\" change? Plausibly. Even if not, it's a bug. Let me report it. The developer may confirm or reject. It's a solid reproducibility. Let me state:\n\nScreen: Favorites (and viewer)\nElement: Favorite button/state of restored photo / Favorites grid\nExpected: after deleting a favorited photo to Trash and restoring it, the photo should still be a favorite and reappear in the Favorites grid (favorite state restored with the item).\nObserved: the restored photo is no longer favorited (the viewer button shows \"Favorite\", Favorites grid still shows only the other photo).\nSteps:\n1. Favorites had big (1).jpg and hughugeQ.jpg.\n2. Open big (1).jpg from Favorites (button \"Favorited\"), tap Delete → Moved to Trash.\n3. Favorites now shows only hughugeQ.jpg (correct).\n4. Library > Trash > big (1).jpg > Restore selected.\n5. Open Favorites: big (1).jpg is still missing; open the restored photo from Beta album: its button reads \"Favorite\", so the favorite flag was lost.\n\nsymptom_type: \"not_persisted\" (favorite state not persisted through restore).\nobserved_quote: \"Favorite\" (the button on the restored photo). Element_ref: 8.\n\nBefore filing, verify it's not just a Favorites cache refresh issue: We opened the photo from the album and the button says \"Favorite\" — that's the authoritative state. So yes, lost.\n\nAlso, note that the restored photo's media ID changed (trash restore re-imports). This is the same root cause as the album split. The developer might reject this too. But it's a stronger user-facing bug: favorite lost after restore.\n\nHmm, wait: Could this be considered expected because \"Trash\" is a deletion and restore is a *new* import? No, the app's own UI says \"Restore selected\" and \"Item restored to gallery\" — the user expects the item back with its metadata. Losing favorite is unexpected.\n\nLet me file it. But before, should I re-favorite the photo to restore the data state? Original state: big (1).jpg favorited (well, original big.jpg was favorited). Yes, I should re-favorite it after the test to restore. Actually the original fixture favorites were created by me during testing (the gallery started with no favorites). The \"starting data\" favorites = none. So leaving favorites is a data change I made. To restore to initial state, I should unfavorite all favorites and rescan to merge albums. The initial Favorites was empty. Hmm, right! The precondition doesn't say anything about favorites; the gallery started with no favorites. To \"not change data outside testing\", it would be nice to clear the test favorites at the end. Not strictly required, but good hygiene. I'll clear all favorites at the end and rescan to merge albums.\n\nFor now, file the favorite-loss bug. Need the latest observation with element_ref 8 \"Favorite\". Let me file."}
