{"type": "thinking", "text": "Now only 5 albums:\n- IrisSeed huge 1\n- IrisSeed big 1\n- Zulu 1\n- apple 1\n- Beta hughugeQ 1\nTotal 5 items. So the restored big (1).jpg REALLY disappeared from the album list! But wait, earlier after restore, we saw the Beta big (1).jpg album card and opened it (\"1 of 1 · big (1).jpg\"). Then we opened Favorites, Albums, etc. Now it's gone.\n\nHmm, maybe the restored big (1).jpg got *re-deleted*? No, Trash is empty. Or maybe the media scan removed it because the file wasn't actually written? Or the album grid's cache is stale after the restore, and the item vanished when the app re-scanned? The Media count also dropped to 5. So the restored file is gone from the app's view entirely. But the file might exist on disk. This smells like the trash-restore is buggy for files that were created via the app's move (generic file URI) — or the restore of a file that was already restored once.\n\nWait, let's recall the history of big (1).jpg:\n- It was created by the first \"Move to album\" of Beta/big.jpg → apple/big (1).jpg (URI external/file/1000000019).\n- Then moved to Beta → Beta/big (1).jpg (maybe another new URI).\n- Then we deleted it to trash and restored it (this test).\n- After restore, it appeared in the Beta album detail (\"1 of 1 · big (1).jpg\") and I opened it.\n- Then I opened Favorites (it wasn't there), opened Albums (it was there as a 1-item Beta card and two Beta cards split), opened it, etc.\n- Now it's gone from Media (5 items) and Albums (5 cards). So the restore was transient; the item vanished later. Maybe a media rescan (triggered by something) removed a broken file row. Or the app's DB removed it on refresh because the file doesn't exist on disk! The restore might have failed to actually restore the file, leaving a MediaStore row that later got cleaned up by the scanner.\n\nHmm! That's a serious bug: restoring a photo shows it restored, but it disappears shortly after (file not actually restored). But is this tied to the particular file created by the app? Possibly.\n\nWait, maybe the restored file was saved to the *IrisSeed* or a different folder and the *Beta* card we saw was stale. Hmm.\n\nActually, let's check the Trash — is it empty? We saw \"Trash is empty\" and toast \"Item restored to gallery\". So the app thinks it's restored.\n\nBut now the media count is 5 and albums sum 5. Which file is missing? The beta big (1).jpg. So the restore didn't persist. That's a data-loss bug. Hmm.\n\nCould the file still be on disk but not indexed? The user could rescan to recover. Let me try \"Rescan media library\" and see if it reappears. That's a good test and will also merge the IrisSeed duplicates. If the file reappears after rescan, then the app's media indexing lost it but the file is fine. If not, the file is gone (restore failed). Let's rescan now.\n\nAlso, the missing Media item might explain why Favorites didn't show the restored favorite — the item was dropped from the Media data source. If the seeded favorites bug is \"favoriting an item that's not in the Media data source doesn't appear in Favorites\", this is a manifestation but requires a broken restore.\n\nLet me rescan (Settings → Storage & Reset) and observe. This will also tell us the final state.\n\nGo Settings icon (element 6). Scroll sequence again."}
